# Consultations whose provider attribution is NOT established
#
# Enforced by check_consultation_provenance (scripts/lib/consultation-provenance.sh).
# Every .md in this directory must either carry a provenance block written by
# scripts/consult.sh, or appear here on a line of its own with a reason.
#
# This register is not a loophole. It is the opposite: an artifact whose
# attribution is unknown is allowed to exist and is NOT allowed to look proven.
# Every entry below is a claim this repository has stopped making.
#
# ── What happened ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# On 2026-07-31, `jcode run -p openai -m gpt-5.6-sol` was found to return
# plausible reports with exit 0 while the tool's own log recorded the request
# being served by DeepSeek. The -p/-m flags are discarded whenever [provider]
# default_provider names an API-key provider; resolution slides to OpenRouter
# and the DEFAULT model serves — which in this repository is the builder.
#
# Measured directly in the two dispatch windows:
#
#     08:07–08:40   803 events   all prv:OpenRouter|mod:deepseek   zero OpenAI
#     10:01–10:15   450 events   all prv:OpenRouter|mod:deepseek   zero OpenAI
#
# ── A correction, because the first version of this file got its facts wrong ─
#
# It cited a per-day count of `endpoint: https://api.openai.com` lines. Those
# lines are `/v1/models` catalog probes, 63 of 66 sitting beside an HTTP 401 —
# the OpenAI *API key* is dead, which `jcode usage` reports plainly. They have
# nothing to do with the OAuth path that serves Sol.
#
# The strict signal is the session tag. Published figure vs. actual:
#
#     07-24    13 vs  9738      07-27    66 vs     0   ← inverted
#     07-25     0 vs    42      07-28     0 vs     0
#     07-26     8 vs  8279      07-30     0 vs   562   ← inverted
#                               07-31     0 vs  1712
#
# An independent reviewer found this on its first pass and named the lesson,
# which is in docs/operator-lessons.md: "a count is not a reading."
#
# ── format ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The filename alone on a line, then an indented reason.

## Established as NOT independent

127-sol.md
    Served by DeepSeek — the same provider as the builder whose code it
    reviewed. Dispatched 08:07 on 2026-07-31; every one of the 803 events in
    that window is tagged prv:OpenRouter|mod:deepseek. PR #127 was merged
    citing this as a cross-provider review; that condition was not met. See
    #135. A re-review under a verified provider is required before the S2
    validator can be said to have passed its tier.

127-sol-round2.md
    Served by DeepSeek. Dispatched 10:01, 450 events, same evidence. This was
    the round that verified round 1's conditions had been met, so the
    verification of the verification is unproven as well.

